{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfxwX91Qbfx8V7HrW1NWN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four steps are done.\n\n1. **Data view:** \"Kibana Sample Data Flights\" has a time field called `timestamp`.\n2. **Dashboard:** \"S4-1d3a0f3e Flights\" has two panels. One is a line chart of flight counts over time. The other is a bar chart of flight counts by `Carrier`.\n3. **Alert rule:** \"S4-1d3a0f3e Cancelled flights\" is an `.es-query` rule on `kibana_sample_data_flights`. It runs every minute and fires when more than 10 documents with `Cancelled: true` appear in a 5-minute window. It was created disabled, so I enabled it.\n4. **Edits and read-back:** I renamed the carrier panel to \"Flights by carrier\". I created it with a temporary title first, so the rename is the only change. Reading the rule back shows it enabled, with status \"ok\".\n\nI didn't re-read the dashboard after the rename. The panel update returned success.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":587,"cache_read_input_tokens":20553,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":587},"output_tokens":345,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0da1e72d-e9d9-58d9-b388-fca8d0eba393","uuid":"d1357a66-7865-4bfa-b5cf-641b12122e4b","timestamp":"2026-10-12T20:03:06.381Z","request_id":"req_011CfxwX8n1ui1K2mLCDLHDq"}
